1
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:06,197
(Raj:)I love this time of the year.

2
00:00:06,368 --> 00:00:09,288
(Raj:)The leaves are turning.
There's a bracing chill in the air.

3
00:00:09,454 --> 00:00:12,084
(Howard:)Plus, there's a whole new crop
of female grad students...

4
00:00:12,249 --> 00:00:16,169
(Howard:)...about to put on just enough winter
weight to make them needy and vulnerable.

5
00:00:18,589 --> 00:00:22,129
(Howard:)That's right, honey, have another calzone.
Daddy can wait.

6
00:00:24,595 --> 00:00:27,515
Isn't there a policy
against dating graduate students?

7
00:00:27,681 --> 00:00:30,021
(Leonard:)No. If you can talk to them,
you can ask them out.

8
00:00:30,184 --> 00:00:31,684
(Raj:)Damn. There's always a catch.

9
00:00:33,103 --> 00:00:34,983
- Hey, guys.
- Hey, Leslie.

10
00:00:35,147 --> 00:00:38,437
(Leslie:)So, dumb-ass, I heard you made
a grad student throw up last night.

11
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:44,113
(Sheldon:)The truth can indeed be a finger down
the throat of those unprepared to hear it.

12
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:46,987
(Sheldon:)But why should I cater
to second-rate minds?

13
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:50,707
(Leslie:)Because first-rate minds
call you "dumb-ass."

14
00:00:52,623 --> 00:00:54,453
(Sheldon:)Oh, yeah? Well...

15
00:00:54,625 --> 00:00:56,545
(Sheldon:)You're a mean person.

16
00:00:57,836 --> 00:00:59,086
Excuse me, Dr. Cooper?

17
00:00:59,463 --> 00:01:02,023
(Girl(arriving):)I'm Ramona Nowitzki.
I was at your talk last night.

